q("ag-016", B, 2, GA, "Why do we need to breathe in air?", "To get oxygen for our bodies to use", [W("To get carbon dioxide for our bodies to use", "reversed", "We give carbon dioxide out."), W("To fill our lungs so that they stay big", "wrong-idea", "We breathe to take in oxygen, not just to fill space."), W("To get water vapour so that we do not need to drink", "wrong-idea", "We still need to drink water.")], ["The body uses oxygen from the air for respiration."], None)
q("ag-017", B, 2, GA, "A cold can of drink is left on a table. Drops of water appear on its outside. Where did the water come from?", "Water vapour in the air", [W("Water that leaked through tiny holes in the can", "wrong-idea", "The can is sealed. The drops come from outside."), W("Oxygen in the air that turned into water", "wrong-gas", "Oxygen does not turn into water."), W("Water that the can made from the cold", "wrong-idea", "Cold does not make water. Water vapour cools and forms drops.")], ["Water vapour in the air touches the cold can and turns back into water."], None)
q("ag-018", B, 2, GA, "A candle burns under a jar standing on a table. After a while the flame goes out. Why?", "The oxygen in the jar has been used up", [W("All the air in the jar has been used up", "air-vs-oxygen", "Only the oxygen is used. Other gases remain."), W("The nitrogen in the jar has been used up", "wrong-gas", "Nitrogen is not used by a burning candle."), W("The jar has too much oxygen", "reversed", "Extra oxygen makes the flame brighter.")], ["A burning candle uses oxygen. When it runs low, the flame goes out."], lambda: bells([(150, 90, 120, "Jar")], "A candle burning under a jar"))
q("ag-019", B, 2, GA, "Two identical candles are lit and covered by jars P and Q. Which candle goes out first?", "The one under jar P, because there is less oxygen in it", [W("The one under jar Q, because it has more oxygen", "reversed", "More oxygen lets a candle burn longer."), W("Both go out at the same time because the flames are the same", "wrong-idea", "The amount of oxygen differs."), W("Neither, because a candle can burn with no air", "wrong-idea", "A flame needs oxygen.")], ["The small jar has less air and so less oxygen. The candle uses it up sooner."], lambda: bells([(90, 70, 90, "P"), (210, 110, 140, "Q")], "Candles under two jars"))
