q("ag-201", C, 3, GA, "A candle burns in a closed jar over water until it goes out. The water rises only a short way up the jar. Why does it not rise further?", "Only the oxygen, about one fifth of air, was used", [W("The water is too heavy to rise higher", "wrong-idea", "The amount of gas lost sets the rise."), W("All the gases in the jar were used up by the candle", "wrong-idea", "Most of the gas in the jar remained."), W("The candle also made oxygen as it burned", "reversed", "A burning candle uses up oxygen.")], ["About 21% of air is oxygen, and the rest stays in the jar."], lambda: trough(0.2, False, caption="Water level after burning"))
q("ag-202", C, 3, GA, "Aiden's jar has a small crack at the top. When he repeats the candle experiment, the water inside hardly rises. Why?", "Air from outside enters through the crack and replaces oxygen", [W("The crack lets in water, so the level is the same inside and outside", "wrong-idea", "The crack is at the top, so air enters, not water."), W("The candle burns more oxygen because of the crack", "wrong-idea", "The crack does not make the candle use more oxygen."), W("The candle burns faster because of the crack, so uses more air", "wrong-idea", "Burning speed does not decide how much gas is lost.")], ["The jar must be airtight for the volume of gas lost to show."], lambda: trough(0, True, caption="A jar over a burning candle"))
